      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can provide general guidance. For a 6-year-old child, the American Academy of Pediatrics recommends starting with a low dose of acetaminophen (such as Tylenol) instead of aspirin. Aspirin should not be given to children under 18 years old due to the risk of Reye's syndrome. For a 6-year-old, start with 1/4 to 1/2 teaspoon of infant acetaminophen (dose depends on the child's weight) every 4-6 hours. Always consult with your pediatrician for personalized advice and to confirm the dosage.",
